+/* 2026-07-31 black-background fix: screen.py's root Gtk.Overlay (class
+ * main_overlay) and its sole overlay child, base_panel's Gtk.Grid (class
+ * main_grid), each resolve background-color to transparent by default --
+ * confirmed live via GtkStyleContext introspection: the toplevel 'window'
+ * node correctly resolves @bg, but main_grid gets its own separate
+ * GdkWindow that starts fully transparent (rgba 0,0,0,0) and, with no
+ * compositor running (raw X11/DRM, no window manager), that renders as
+ * solid black instead of showing the window bg through it -- visible as a
+ * black background behind every button/plaque on every panel. Targeted
+ * classes rather than a blanket 'grid'/'overlay' type selector: plain
+ * Gtk.Grid is used ~70 other places in the codebase (some nested inside
+ * intentionally differently-colored ancestors) and job_status.py has its
+ * own Gtk.Overlay for a progress indicator over a thumbnail image, where
+ * painting an opaque @bg would visibly break that overlay. */
+.main_overlay,
+.main_grid,
 list row,
 treeview.view,
 window {
